      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Selecting a node inside a graph must not, by itself, change which graph anchors the workspace layout",
        "body": "Bug report: \"sometimes when I click on a graph, it moves the entire graph across the workspace.\"\n\nRoot cause, traced and confirmed by static analysis (not yet live-reproduced):\n\n`components/GraphEditor/hooks/useGraphWorkspace.js`'s `activate(instanceId, nodeId)` sets THREE unrelated things in one call:\n1. `store.current.activeGraphInstanceId` — which graph's editing session is live (a real dependency: a passive graph is read-only via PassiveGraph, so selecting a node inside it does need this).\n2. `store.current.focusedGraphInstanceId` — read by `reflowWorkspaceInstances()` in `graphWorkspace.js` as the anchor for its force-directed layout, AND by `presentWorkspaceInstances()` to decide who renders at full expanded size instead of a collapsed card.\n3. `live.current.state.setFocusedNodeId(nodeId)` / `setSelectedNodeIds([nodeId])` — which node is selected inside that graph's own canvas.\n\n`components/GraphEditor/components/WorkspaceLayer.js`'s `activateAt` hit-tests the click against the graph's own node positions. Land on a node -> calls `workspace.activate(instance.instanceId, node.id)`, the full three-way call. Land on empty card space -> only `selectInstances()`, no focus change.\n\nSo: whether a click lands a few pixels onto a node or a few pixels off it decides whether `focusedGraphInstanceId` (and therefore the reflow anchor) changes at all. When it does change, every OTHER open, ready graph that the user hasn't hand-dragged (`instance.manuallyPlaced === false`, the default) gets pushed through `reflowWorkspaceInstances()`'s 200+30 iterations of force-directed relaxation and resettles around the new anchor — visibly relocating a graph the user never touched. That's the reported symptom.\n\n`focusWorkspace()` already proves `activeGraphInstanceId` and `focusedGraphInstanceId` can diverge (it clears the latter, keeps the former) — this isn't fighting the model, it's completing a distinction the code already half-draws.\n\nConstraint: commits eb950a55/e2a77db8/f68272b9 (see docs/release-readiness.md) deliberately made load/create/reopen ALSO focus, where previously only the explicit Focus button did. This fix must not roll that back — it's specifically about the implicit node-click-inside-a-passive-graph path, not about narrowing focus everywhere.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Clicking a node inside a passive (non-active, non-focused) graph selects that node and makes its graph the active editing session, without changing focusedGraphInstanceId",
          "A graph that becomes active this way does not become the reflow anchor and does not force other open graphs to resettle",
          "The explicit Focus button, and the existing load/create/reopen-focuses behavior, are unchanged — they still set focusedGraphInstanceId as they do today",
          "A live or automated repro (two open graphs, click a node in the non-anchor one) shows the other graph no longer relocates"
        ],
