      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Add a node-select path that does not touch focusedGraphInstanceId",
        "body": "In useGraphWorkspace.js, split what activate() currently does into two primitives:\n- activateInstance(instanceId) — today's full behavior: sets activeGraphInstanceId AND focusedGraphInstanceId, centers camera. Used by deliberate focus (the Focus button) and the existing load/create/reopen-focuses paths. Keep its call sites there unchanged.\n- selectNodeInInstance(instanceId, nodeId) — new, narrower: sets activeGraphInstanceId (so the node can actually be selected/edited), sets the node focus/selection state, but leaves focusedGraphInstanceId untouched if the instance isn't already the focused one.\n\nCamera behavior is an open question (see the open question node) — decide there whether selectNodeInInstance should still call centerOnInstance.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "useGraphWorkspace.js exposes both activateInstance and selectNodeInInstance (naming negotiable)",
          "selectNodeInInstance never writes store.current.focusedGraphInstanceId",
          "Existing callers that want full focus (Focus button, load/create/reopen) call activateInstance unchanged"
        ],
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
